ge population of Begonia edulis Lévl., 1909 (Figure 31 A, B). There are droplets of water in some places at half way or near the bottom. The blind beetles were discovered lower half of the cave (Figure 31 C). Apart from D. (s. str.) mingruoae n. sp., Dongodytes (Dongodytodes) sp. and Eutrichodemus millipede species also occur in this limestone cave.","","text","",""]]},"NKLSR":{"d":[["United States","US","iso","native",""],["United States","US","iso","native",""],["United States","US","iso","native",""],["United States","US","iso","native",""]]},"NW8X5":{"d":[["Locality of the original isolate: Russia","","text","",""]]},"NXQS":{"d":[["","CBD","tdwg","",""],["","CHH","tdwg","",""],["","MLY","tdwg","",""],["","SUM","tdwg","",""],["","THA","tdwg","",""],["","VIE","tdwg","",""]]},"P5LNK":{"d":[["","CO","iso","native",""]]},"P6TZV":{"d":[["Global","","text","native","vulnerable"]]},"P8LV":{"d":[["Greece","","text","native",""]]},"P9LBS":{"d":[["Middle America","","text","",""]]},"PQ7DN":{"d":[["","UKR-UK","tdwg","",""]]},"PVP4":{"d":[["Caribbean","","text","",""]]},"Q5P4":{"d":[["","BG","iso","native",""],["","JO","iso","native",""]]},"QP9P":{"d":[["Neotropical(Mexico:Veracruz)","","text","",""]]},"RPV2":{"d":[["Australasia","","text","native",""]]},"RQ4S":{"d":[["Australasia","","text","native",""]]},"RQ52":{"d":[["Australasia","","text","native",""]]},"RQY86":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"S2VVY":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"S2VW8":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"SFGJ":{"d":[["","NEP-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Nepal","","text","native",""]]},"SM5HM":{"d":[["Distribution and biology. Rhyacophila parvicauda sp. nov. was collected only from a few small headwater streams in a mountain area of Shikoku (Fig. 9 D). This species tends to be distributed at rather higher altitude than R. inazui and R. vesperalis in the same river systems. Adults of this species were collected from late May to August. Japanese name. Hime-kuremensu-nagare-tobikera.",